40\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-CassidyDefeat-40\" id=\"mwBiM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBiQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBiU\">[</span>26<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBiY\">]</span></span></a></sup></td></tr>\n<tr id=\"mwBic\">\n<th id=\"mwBig\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_Senate_election_in_Texas\" title=\"2026 United States Senate election in Texas\" id=\"mwBik\">Texas</a></th>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\" about=\"#mwt1201\" typeof=\"mw:ExpandedAttrs\" id=\"mwBis\" data-mw='{\"attribs\":[[{\"txt\":\"style\",\"html\":\"&lt;span about=\\\"#mwt1200\\\" typeof=\\\"mw:Transclusion\\\" id=\\\"mwBio\\\" data-mw=&apos;{\\\"parts\\\":[{\\\"template\\\":{\\\"target\\\":{\\\"wt\\\":\\\"Party shading/Republican\\\",\\\"href\\\":\\\"./Template:Party_shading/Republican\\\"},\\\"params\\\":{},\\\"i\\\":0}}]}&apos;>style=\\\"color:black; background-color:&lt;/span>&lt;span typeof=\\\"mw:Nowiki\\\" about=\\\"#mwt1200\\\">&lt;/span>&lt;span about=\\\"#mwt1200\\\">#FFB6B6\\\"&lt;/span>\"},{\"html\":\"\"}]]}'><span data-sort-value=\"Cornyn, John\" about=\"#mwt1198\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBiw\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"sortname\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sortname\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"John\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Cornyn\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Cornyn\" title=\"John Cornyn\">John Cornyn</a></span></span></span><link rel=\"mw:PageProp/Category\" href=\"./Category:Articles_with_hCards\" about=\"#mwt1198\" id=\"mwBi0\"/></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\" id=\"mwBi4\">74</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\" id=\"mwBi8\">2002</td>\n<td id=\"mwBjA\">TBD</td>\n<td id=\"mwBjE\"><sup about=\"#mwt1204\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-CornynDefeat_41-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"CornynDefeat\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-CornynDefeat-41\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-CornynDefeat-41\" id=\"mwBjI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBjM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBjQ\">[</span>27<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBjU\">]</span></span></a></sup></td></tr>\n</tbody></table><!--\n\n===Post&#x2D;election changes===\nOne Democrat and one Republican resigned shortly before the end of the 119th Congress. All are to be replaced by appointees.\n{| class=\"wikitable sortable plainrowheaders\"\n|&#x2D;\n! scope=\"col\" |State\n! scope=\"col\" |Senator\n! scope=\"col\" |Age at <br /&#x3E; end of term\n! scope=\"col\" |Assumed <br /&#x3E; office\n! scope=\"col\" |Replaced by\n! scope=\"col\" |{{Abbr|Ref|Reference}}\n|&#x2D;\n! Minnesota<br/&#x3E;(Class 1)\n| {{Party shading/DFL}} | {{sortname|Amy|Klobuchar}}\n| style=\"text&#x2D;align:center\" | 66\n| style=\"text&#x2D;align:center\" | 2007\n| {{Party shading/DFL}} | TBD\n| \n|&#x2D;\n! Tennessee<br/&#x3E;(Class 1)\n| {{Party shading/Republican}} | {{sortname|Marsha|Blackburn}}\n| style=\"text&#x2D;align:center\" | 74\n| style=\"text&#x2D;align:center\" | 2019\n| {{Party shading/Republican}} | TBD\n|\n|}\n-->\n\n</section></section><section data-mw-section-id=\"10\" id=\"mwBjY\" aria-labelledby=\"Predictions\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Predictions\">Predictions</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_Senate_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Predictions\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n\n<p id=\"mwBjc\">Multiple sites and political pundits have published predictions of competitive seats. These predictions have considered factors such as the strength of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Incumbent\" title=\"Incumbent\" id=\"mwBjg\">incumbent</a> (if the incumbent was running for reelection) and the other candidates, and the state's partisan lean, reflected in part by the state's <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cook_Partisan_Voting_Index\" title=\"Cook Partisan Voting Index\" id=\"mwBjk\">Cook Partisan Voting Index</a> rating. The predictions typically assign ratings to each seat, indicating the predicted advantage that a party had in winning that seat. Most election predictors use:</p>\n<ul id=\"mwBjo\"><li id=\"mwBjs\">\"<u id=\"mwBjw\">tossup</u>\": no advantage</li>\n<li id=\"mwBj0\">\"<u id=\"mwBj4\">tilt</u>\" (used by some predictors): advantage that is not quite as strong as \"lean\"</li>\n<li id=\"mwBj8\">\"<u id=\"mwBkA\">lean</u>\": slight advantage</li>\n<li id=\"mwBkE\">\"<u id=\"mwBkI\">likely</u>\": significant, but surmountable, advantage</li>\n<li id=\"mwBkM\">\"<u id=\"mwBkQ\">safe</u>\" or \"<u id=\"mwBkU\">solid</u>\": near-certain chance of victory<!-- Colors and sorting:\n\nIn many cases, the incumbent has yet to say their intention of running for another term. If an incumbent intends to retire then place \"<br /&#x3E;{{Small|(Retiring)}}\" after the incumbent's name.\n\nSee [[Template:USRaceRating]] for how to apply rating.\n\n--></li></ul>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1205\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBkY\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"sticky header\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sticky_header\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1305414688\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" about=\"#mwt1206\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"template:sticky header/styles.css\"}}'>@media screen and (min-width:640px){.mw-parser-output .sticky-header>thead>tr:first-child,.mw-parser-output .sticky-header>caption+tbody>tr:first-child,.mw-parser-output .sticky-header>tbody:first-child>tr:first-child,.mw-parser-output .sticky-header-multi>thead{position:sticky;top:0;z-i