Democratic</a></td></tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"4\"><hr/></td></tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #DCDCDC;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Seth_Bodnar_-_President_at_University_of_Montana_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Seth_Bodnar_-_President_at_University_of_Montana_(cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Seth_Bodnar_-_President_at_University_of_Montana_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Seth_Bodnar_-_President_at_University_of_Montana_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Seth_Bodnar_-_President_at_University_of_Montana_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Seth_Bodnar_-_President_at_University_of_Montana_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1651\" data-file-height=\"2233\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"100\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #fed000;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/120px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/250px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"3\" data-file-height=\"4\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"136\" width=\"102\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seth_Bodnar\" title=\"Seth Bodnar\">Seth Bodnar</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Kyle Austin</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Independent_politician\" title=\"Independent politician\">Independent</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Libertarian_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Libertarian Party (United States)\">Libertarian</a></td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Montana\" title=\"List of United States senators from Montana\">U.S. senator</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steve_Daines\" title=\"Steve Daines\">Steve Daines</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3362\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFCU\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 United States Senate election in Montana\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt3363\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt3362\" id=\"mwFCY\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_Senate_election_in_Montana\" title=\"2026 United States Senate election in Montana\">2026 United States Senate election in Montana</a></div>\n\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3364\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFCc\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"See also\",\"href\":\"./Template:See_also\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"List of United States senators from Montana\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt3365\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt3364\" id=\"mwFCg\">See also: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Montana\" title=\"List of United States senators from Montana\">List of United States senators from Montana</a></div>\n<p id=\"mwFCk\">Two-term Republican <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steve_Daines\" title=\"Steve Daines\" id=\"mwFCo\">Steve Daines</a> was <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_United_States_Senate_election_in_Montana\" title=\"2020 United States Senate election in Montana\" id=\"mwFCs\">reelected in 2020</a> with 55% of the vote. On March 4, 2026, Daines announced he would not seek reelection. The same day, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Attorney\" title=\"United States Attorney\" id=\"mwFCw\">U.S. Attorney</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kurt_Alme\" title=\"Kurt Alme\" id=\"mwFC0\">Kurt Alme</a> announced his candidacy and immediately won Daines's endorsement.<sup about=\"#mwt3368\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-244\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-244\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-244\" id=\"mwFC4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFC8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFDA\">[</span>220<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFDE\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwFDI\">Former <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montana_House_of_Representatives\" title=\"Montana House of Representatives\" id=\"mwFDM\">state Representative</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reilly_Neill\" title=\"Reilly Neill\" id=\"mwFDQ\">Reilly Neill</a> ran for the Democratic nomination,<sup about=\"#mwt3371\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Neill_245-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Neill\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Neill-245\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Neill-245\" id=\"mwFDU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFDY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFDc\">[</span>221<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFDg\">]</span></span></a></sup> but was defeated in the Democratic primary by former <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Air_Force\" title=\"U.S. Air Force\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwFDk\">U.S. Air Force</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lieutenant_Colonel\" title=\"Lieutenant Colonel\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwFDo\">Lieutenant Colonel</a> Alani Bankhead in a major <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Upset_(competition)\" title=\"Upset (competition)\" id=\"mwFDs\">upset</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt3374\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-246\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-246\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-246\" id=\"mwFDw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFD0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFD4\">[</span>222<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFD8\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwFEA\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seth_Bodnar\" title=\"Seth Bodnar\" id=\"mwFEE\">Seth Bodnar</a>, the president of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/University_of_Montana\" title=\"University of Montana\" id=\"mwFEI\">University of Montana</a> until January 2026, is running as an independent candidate.<sup about=\"#mwt3377\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-247\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-247\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-247\" id=\"mwFEM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFEQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFEU\">[</span>223<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFEY\">]</span></span></a></sup> Former U.S. Senator <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jon_Tester\" title=\"Jon Tester\" id=\"mwFEc\">Jon Tester</a> endorsed Bodnar, surprising many and angering many Democrats.<sup about=\"#mwt3380\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-248\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-248\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-248\" id=\"mwFEg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFEk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFEo\">[</span>224<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFEs\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt3381\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFEw\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"40\" id=\"mwFE0\" aria-labelledby=\"Nebraska\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Nebraska\">Nebraska</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_Senate_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=40\" title=\"Edit section: Nebraska\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3382\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFE4\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"Nebraska election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"Nebraska\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2024 United States Senate special election in Nebraska\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2024\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2032 United States Senate election in Nebraska\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"&apos;&apos;2032&apos;&apos;\"},\"election_date\":{\"wt\":\"&lt;!--Don&apos;t need election date in section infoboxes when the date is the same as in the article&apos;s main infobox.-->\"},\"image_size\":{\"wt\":\"125x136px\"},\"turnout\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"Sen. Pete Ricketts official portrait, 118th Congress (cropped).jpg\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Pete Ricketts]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"Osborn Headshot 2 (cropped) (cropped).jpg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"[[Dan Osborn]]\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Independent politician\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_image\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_size\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_caption\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"U.S. Senator\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Pete Ricketts]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt3383\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt3384\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt3385\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt3382\" id=\"mwFE8\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">Nebraska election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Nebraska.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Flag_of_Nebraska.svg/60px-Flag_of_Nebraska.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Flag_of_Nebraska.svg/120px-Flag_of_Nebraska.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"750\" data-file-height=\"450\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"30\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_United_States_Senate_special_election_in_Nebraska\" title=\"2024 United States Senate special election in Nebraska\">2024</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><i>2032</i><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Sen._Pete_Ricketts_official_portrait,_118th_Congress_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Sen._Pete_Ricketts_official_portrait,_118th_Congress_(cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Sen._Pete_Ricketts_official_portrait%2C_118th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Sen._Pete_Ricketts_official_portrait%2C_118th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Sen._Pete_Ricketts_official_portrait%2C_118th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Sen._Pete_Ricketts_official_portrait%2C_118th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1173\" data-file-height=\"1614\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"99\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #DCDCDC;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Osborn_Headshot_2_(cropped)_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Osborn_Headshot_2_(cropped)_(cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Osborn_Headshot_2_%28cropped%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Osborn_Headshot_2_%28cropped%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Osborn_Headshot_2_%28cropped%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Osborn_Headshot_2_%28cropped%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1481\" data-file-height=\"1974\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"102\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pete_Ricketts\" title=\"Pete Ricketts\">Pete Ricketts</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dan_Osborn\" title=\"Dan Osborn\">Dan Osborn</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Independent_politician\" title=\"Independent politician\">Independent</a></td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Nebraska\" title=\"List of United States senators from Nebraska\">U.S. senator</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pete_Ricketts\" title=\"Pete Ricketts\">Pete Ricketts</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3386\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFFA\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 United States Senate election in Nebraska\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt3387\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt3386\" id=\"mwFFE\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_Senate_election_in_Nebraska\" title=\"2026 United States Senate election in Nebraska\">2026 United States Senate election in Nebraska</a></div>\n\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3388\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFFI\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"See also\",\"href\":\"./Template:See_also\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"List of United States senators from Nebraska\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt3389\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt3388\" id=\"mwFFM\">See also: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Nebraska\" title=\"List of United States senators from Nebraska\">List of United States senators from Nebraska</a></div>\n<p id=\"mwFFQ\">Two-term Republican <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ben_Sasse\" title=\"Ben Sasse\" id=\"mwFFU\">Ben Sasse</a> resigned early in the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/118th_United_States_Congress\" title=\"118th United States Congress\" id=\"mwFFY\">118th Congress</a> to become president of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/University_of_Florida\" title=\"University of Florida\" id=\"mwFFc\">University of Florida</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt3392\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-249\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-249\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-249\" id=\"mwFFg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFFk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFFo\">[</span>225<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFFs\">]</span></span></a></sup> On January 12, 2023, Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jim_Pillen\" title=\"Jim Pillen\" id=\"mwFFw\">Jim Pillen</a> appointed former governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pete_Ricketts\" title=\"Pete Ricketts\" id=\"mwFF0\">Pete Ricketts</a> as senator.<sup about=\"#mwt3395\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-250\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-250\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-250\" id=\"mwFF4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFF8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFGA\">[</span>226<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFGE\">]</span></span></a></sup> Ricketts won the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_United_States_Senate_special_election_in_Nebraska\" title=\"2024 United States Senate special election in Nebraska\" id=\"mwFGI\">2024 special election</a> to complete Sasse's term, defeating college professor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Preston_Love_Jr.\" title=\"Preston Love Jr.\" id=\"mwFGM\">Preston Love Jr.</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt3398\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-251\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-251\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-251\" id=\"mwFGQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFGU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFGY\">[</span>227<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFGc\">]</span></span></a></sup> and is now running for reelection to his first full term.<sup about=\"#mwt3401\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-252\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-252\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-252\" id=\"mwFGg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFGk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFGo\">[</span>228<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFGs\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwFGw\">Former labor union leader <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dan_Osborn\" title=\"Dan Osborn\" id=\"mwFG0\">Dan Osborn</a>, who challenged Republican <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deb_Fischer\" title=\"Deb Fischer\" id=\"mwFG4\">Deb Fischer</a> for <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Nebraska\" title=\"2024 United States Senate election in Nebraska\" id=\"mwFG8\">Nebraska's Class I Senate seat</a>, has announced an independent bid.<sup about=\"#mwt3404\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Osborn_127-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Osborn\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Osborn-127\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Osborn-127\" id=\"mwFHA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFHE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFHI\">[</span>104<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFHM\">]</span></span></a></sup></p> \n\n<p id=\"mwFHQ\">The <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nebraska_Democratic_Party\" title=\"Nebraska Democratic Party\" id=\"mwFHU\">Nebraska Democratic Party</a> has declined to recruit a Democratic challenger to Ricketts,<sup about=\"#mwt3407\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-253\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-253\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-253\" id=\"mwFHY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFHc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFHg\">[</span>229<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFHk\">]</span></span></a></sup> and the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jane_Kleeb\" title=\"Jane Kleeb\" id=\"mwFHo\">party's chair</a> has endorsed Osborn.<sup about=\"#mwt3410\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-254\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-254\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-254\" id=\"mwFHs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFHw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFH0\">[</span>230<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFH4\">]</span></span></a></sup> Other candidates filed for the Democratic primary, raising concern that their campaigns could split the vote and weaken Osborn's support in the general election,<sup about=\"#mwt3413\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-:1_255-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\":1\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:1-255\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-:1-255\" id=\"mwFH8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFIA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFIE\">[</span>231<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFII\">]</span></span></a></sup> but retired pharmacy technician Cindy Burbank won the Democratic primary and said she intended to withdraw from the general election if she sees no clear path to victory.<sup about=\"#mwt3416\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-256\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-256\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-256\" id=\"mwFIM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFIQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFIU\">[</span>232<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFIY\">]</span></span></a></sup> She officially withdrew from the race on July 17.<sup about=\"#mwt3419\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-257\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-257\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-257\" id=\"mwFIc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFIg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFIk\">[</span>233<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFIo\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt3420\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFIs\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"41\" id=\"mwFIw\" aria-labelledby=\"New_Hampshire\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"New_Hampshire\">New Hampshire</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_Senate_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=41\" title=\"Edit section: New Hampshire\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3421\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFI0\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"New Hampshire election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"New Hampshire\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2020 United States Senate election in New Hampshire\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2020\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2032 United States Senate election in New Hampshire\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"&apos;&apos;2032&apos;&apos;\"},\"image_size\":{\"wt\":\"125x136px\"},\"turnout\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"Chris Pappas, official portrait - 2022 (cropped 2).png\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Chris Pappas (American politician)|Chris Pappas]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"John E. Sununu (cropped 2).jpg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"[[John E. Sununu]]\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_image\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_size\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_caption\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"U.S. Senator\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Jeanne Shaheen]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt3422\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt3423\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt3424\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt3421\" id=\"mwFI4\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">New Hampshire election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_New_Hampshire.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Flag_of_New_Hampshire.svg/60px-Flag_of_New_Hampshire.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Flag_of_New_Hampshire.svg/120px-Flag_of_New_Hampshire.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"660\" data-file-height=\"440\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"33\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Hampshire\" title=\"2020 United States Senate election in New Hampshire\">2020</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><i>2032</i><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Chris_Pappas,_official_portrait_-_2022_(cropped_2).png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Chris_Pappas,_official_portrait_-_2022_(cropped_2).png\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Chris_Pappas%2C_official_portrait_-_2022_%28cropped_2%29.png/120px-Chris_Pappas%2C_official_portrait_-_2022_%28cropped_2%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Chris_Pappas%2C_official_portrait_-_2022_%28cropped_2%29.png/250px-Chris_Pappas%2C_official_portrait_-_2022_%28cropped_2%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"271\" data-file-height=\"361\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"102\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:John_E._Sununu_(cropped_2).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:John_E._Sununu_(cropped_2).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/John_E._Sununu_%28cropped_2%29.jpg/120px-John_E._Sununu_%28cropped_2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/John_E._Sununu_%28cropped_2%29.jpg/250px-John_E._Sununu_%28cropped_2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1538\" data-file-height=\"2051\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"102\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Pappas_(American_politician)\" title=\"Chris Pappas (American politician)\">Chris Pappas</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_E._Sununu\" title=\"John E. Sununu\">John E. Sununu</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_New_Hampshire\" title=\"List of United States senators from New Hampshire\">U.S. senator</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jeanne_Shaheen\" title=\"Jeanne Shaheen\">Jeanne Shaheen</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3425\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFI8\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 United States Senate election in New Hampshire\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt3426\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt3425\" id=\"mwFJA\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Hampshire\" title=\"2026 United States Senate election in New Hampshire\">2026 United States Senate election in New Hampshire</a></div>\n\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3427\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFJE\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"See also\",\"href\":\"./Template:See_also\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"List of United States senators from New Hampshire\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt3428\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt3427\" id=\"mwFJI\">See also: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_New_Hampshire\" title=\"List of United States senators from New Hampshire\">List of United States senators from New Hampshire</a></div>\n\n<p id=\"mwFJM\">Three-term <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\" id=\"mwFJQ\">Democrat</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jeanne_Shaheen\" title=\"Jeanne Shaheen\" id=\"mwFJU\">Jeanne Shaheen</a> was <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Hampshire\" title=\"2020 United States Senate election in New Hampshire\" id=\"mwFJY\">reelected in 2020</a> with 56.6% of the vote. On March 12, 2025, Shaheen announced that she would not seek reelection to a fourth term.<sup about=\"#mwt3431\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Shaheen_36-2\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Shaheen\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Shaheen-36\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Shaheen-36\" id=\"mwFJc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFJg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFJk\">[</span>23<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFJo\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwFJs\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Representative\" title=\"U.S. Representative\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwFJw\">U.S. Representative</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Pappas_(American_politician)\" title=\"Chris Pappas (American politician)\" id=\"mwFJ0\">Chris Pappas</a><sup about=\"#mwt3432\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Pappas_129-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Pappas\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Pappas-129\" id=\"mwFJ4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFJ8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFKA\">[</span>106<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFKE\">]</span></span></a></sup> defeated <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Hampshire_Democratic_Party\" title=\"New Hampshire Democratic Party\" id=\"mwFKI\">New Hampshire Democratic Party</a> rules committee member Karishma Manzur<sup about=\"#mwt3435\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Manzur_258-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Manzur\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Manzur-258\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Manzur-258\" id=\"mwFKM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFKQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFKU\">[</span>234<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFKY\">]</span></span></a></sup> to win the Democratic nomination on September 8.<sup about=\"#mwt3438\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-:9_259-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\":9\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:9-259\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-:9-259\" id=\"mwFKc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFKg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFKk\">[</span>235<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFKo\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwFKs\">Former U.S. Senator <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_E._Sununu\" title=\"John E. Sununu\" id=\"mwFKw\">John E. Sununu</a> won the Republican nomination on September 8, defeating former <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Massachusetts\" title=\"Massachusetts\" id=\"mwFK0\">Massachusetts</a> U.S. Senator and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Ambassador_to_New_Zealand_and_Samoa\" title=\"U.S. Ambassador to New Zealand and Samoa\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwFK4\">U.S. Ambassador to New Zealand and Samoa</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scott_Brown_(politician)\" title=\"Scott Brown (politician)\" id=\"mwFK8\">Scott Brown.</a><sup about=\"#mwt3439\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-:9_259-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\":9\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-:9-259\" id=\"mwFLA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFLE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFLI\">[</span>235<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFLM\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt3442\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-nh_260-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"nh\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-nh-260\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-nh-260\" id=\"mwFLQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFLU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFLY\">[</span>236<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFLc\">]</span></span></a></sup> Both have previously lost Senate races to Shaheen: Sununu in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2008_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Hampshire\" title=\"2008 United States Senate election in New Hampshire\" id=\"mwFLg\">2008</a> and Brown in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2014_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Hampshire\" title=\"2014 United States Senate election in New Hampshire\" id=\"mwFLk\">2014</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt3443\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-JohnSununu_79-2\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"JohnSununu\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-JohnSununu-79\" id=\"mwFLo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFLs\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFLw\">[</span>56<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFL0\">]</span></span></a></sup> Sununu's brother, former <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_New_Hampshire\" title=\"Governor of New Hampshire\" id=\"mwFL4\">Governor</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Sununu\" title=\"Chris Sununu\" id=\"mwFL8\">Chris Sununu</a>, declined to run.<sup about=\"#mwt3446\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-261\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-261\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-261\" id=\"mwFMA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFME\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFMI\">[</span>237<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFMM\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt3447\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFMQ\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"42\" id=\"mwFMU\" aria-labelledby=\"New_Jersey\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"New_Jersey\">New Jersey</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_Senate_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=42\" title=\"Edit section: New Jersey\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3448\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFMY\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"New Jersey election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"New Jersey\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2020 United States Senate election in New Jersey\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2020\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2032 United States Senate election in New Jersey\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"&apos;&apos;2032&apos;&apos;\"},\"image_size\":{\"wt\":\"125x136px\"},\"turnout\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"Cory Booker, official portrait (119th Congress) (cropped).jpg\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Cory Booker]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"3x4.svg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"Justin Murphy\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_image\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_size\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_caption\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"U.S. Senator\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Cory Booker]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt3449\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt3450\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt3451\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt3448\" id=\"mwFMc\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">New Jersey election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_New_Jersey.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Flag_of_New_Jersey.svg/60px-Flag_of_New_Jersey.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Flag_of_New_Jersey.svg/120px-Flag_of_New_Jersey.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"1000\" data-file-height=\"600\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"30\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Jersey\" title=\"2020 United States Senate election in New Jersey\">2020</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><i>2032</i><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Cory_Booker,_official_portrait_(119th_Congress)_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Cory_Booker,_official_portrait_(119th_Congress)_(cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Cory_Booker%2C_official_portrait_%28119th_Congress%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Cory_Booker%2C_official_portrait_%28119th_Congress%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Cory_Booker%2C_official_portrait_%28119th_Congress%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Cory_Booker%2C_official_portrait_%28119th_Congress%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"2853\" data-file-height=\"3804\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"102\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/120px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/250px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"3\" data-file-height=\"4\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"136\" width=\"102\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cory_Booker\" title=\"Cory Booker\">Cory Booker</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Justin Murphy</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_New_Jersey\" title=\"List of United States senators from New Jersey\">U.S. senator</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cory_Booker\" title=\"Cory Booker\">Cory Booker</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3452\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFMg\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 United States Senate election in New Jersey\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt3453\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt3452\" id=\"mwFMk\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Jersey\" title=\"2026 United States Senate election in New Jersey\">2026 United States Senate election in New Jersey</a></div>\n\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3454\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFMo\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"See also\",\"href\":\"./Template:See_also\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"List of United States senators from New Jersey\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt3455\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt3454\" id=\"mwFMs\">See also: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_New_Jersey\" title=\"List of United States senators from New Jersey\">List of United States senators from New Jersey</a></div>\n<p id=\"mwFMw\">Two-term Democrat <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cory_Booker\" title=\"Cory Booker\" id=\"mwFM0\">Cory Booker</a> was <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Jersey\" title=\"2020 United States Senate election in New Jersey\" id=\"mwFM4\">reelected in 2020</a> with 57.2% of the vote and is running for reelection to a third full term.<sup about=\"#mwt3458\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-BookerRunning_262-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"BookerRunning\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BookerRunning-262\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-BookerRunning-262\" id=\"mwFM8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFNA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFNE\">[</span>238<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFNI\">]</span></span></a></sup> Booker won the Democratic nomination unopposed, as he was the only candidate to submit the required number of signatures to appear on the primary ballot.<sup about=\"#mwt3461\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-263\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-263\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-263\" id=\"mwFNM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFNQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFNU\">[</span>239<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFNY\">]</span></span></a></sup></p><p id=\"mwFNc\">\n\nOn June 2, 2026, former <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tabernacle_Township,_New_Jersey\" title=\"Tabernacle Township, New Jersey\" id=\"mwFNg\">Tabernacle</a> Mayor Justin Murphy, a Navy veteran and attorney, won the Republican nomination<sup about=\"#mwt3465\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-264\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-264\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-264\" id=\"mwFNk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFNo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFNs\">[</span>240<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFNw\">]</span></span></a></sup> with 33% of the vote, defeating physician Robert Lebovics, U.S. Army combat veteran Richard Tabor, and former <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/News_12_Networks\" title=\"News 12 Networks\" id=\"mwFN0\">News 12</a> reporter Alex Zdan.<sup about=\"#mwt3468\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-265\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-265\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-265\" id=\"mwFN4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFN8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFOA\">[</span>241<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFOE\">]</span></span></a></sup></p><div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt3462\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFOI\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"43\" id=\"mwFOM\" aria-labelledby=\"New_Mexico\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"New_Mexico\">New Mexico</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_Senate_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=43\" title=\"Edit section: New Mexico\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3469\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFOQ\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"New Mexico election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"New Mexico\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2020 United States Senate election in New Mexico\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2020\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2032 United States Senate election in New Mexico\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"&apos;&apos;2032&apos;&apos;\"},\"image_size\":{\"wt\":\"125x136px\"},\"turnout\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"Ben Ray Luján, official portrait (119th Congress) (cropped)1.jpg\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Ben Ray Luján]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"3x4.svg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"Larry Marker\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_image\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_size\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_caption\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"U.S. Senator\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Ben Ray Luján]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt3470\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt3471\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt3472\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt3469\" id=\"mwFOU\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">New Mexico election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_New_Mexico.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Flag_of_New_Mexico.svg/60px-Flag_of_New_Mexico.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Flag_of_New_Mexico.svg/120px-Flag_of_New_Mexico.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"1800\" data-file-height=\"1200\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"33\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Mexico\" title=\"2020 United States Senate election in New Mexico\">2020</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><i>2032</i><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Ben_Ray_Luján,_official_portrait_(119th_Congress)_(cropped)1.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Ben_Ray_Luján,_official_portrait_(119th_Congress)_(cropped)1.jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Ben_Ray_Luj%C3%A1n%2C_official_portrait_%28119th_Congress%29_%28cropped%291.jpg/120px-Ben_Ray_Luj%C3%A1n%2C_official_portrait_%28119th_Congress%29_%28cropped%291.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Ben_Ray_Luj%C3%A1n%2C_official_portrait_%28119th_Congress%29_%28cropped%291.jpg/250px-Ben_Ray_Luj%C3%A1n%2C_official_portrait_%28119th_Congress%29_%28cropped%291.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"2850\" data-file-height=\"3414\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"113\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/120px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/250px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"3\" data-file-height=\"4\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"136\" width=\"102\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ben_Ray_Luján\" title=\"Ben Ray Luján\">Ben Ray Luján</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Larry Marker</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_New_Mexico\" title=\"List of United States senators from New Mexico\">U.S. senator</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ben_Ray_Luján\" title=\"Ben Ray Luján\">Ben Ray Luján</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3473\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFOY\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 United States Senate election in New Mexico\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt3474\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt3473\" id=\"mwFOc\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Mexico\" title=\"2026 United States Senate election in New Mexico\">2026 United States Senate election in New Mexico</a></div>\n\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3475\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFOg\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"See also\",\"href\":\"./Template:See_also\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"List of United States senators from New Mexico\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt3476\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt3475\" id=\"mwFOk\">See also: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_New_Mexico\" title=\"List of United States senators from New Mexico\">List of United States senators from New Mexico</a></div>\n<p id=\"mwFOo\">One-term Democrat <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ben_Ray_Luján\" title=\"Ben Ray Luján\" id=\"mwFOs\">Ben Ray Luján</a> was <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Mexico\" title=\"2020 United States Senate election in New Mexico\" id=\"mwFOw\">elected in 2020</a> with 51.7% of the vote. On April 23, 2025, Luján announced that he would seek a second term.<sup about=\"#mwt3479\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-BRL_266-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"BRL\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BRL-266\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-BRL-266\" id=\"mwFO0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFO4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFO8\">[</span>242<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFPA\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwFPE\">Christopher Heuvel, the only Republican to file, was disqualified for failing to meet ballot requirements.<sup about=\"#mwt3482\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-267\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-267\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-267\" id=\"mwFPI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFPM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFPQ\">[</span>243<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFPU\">]</span></span></a></sup> Former oil and gas operator Larry Marker subsequently qualified for the Republican primary as a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Write-in_candidate\" title=\"Write-in candidate\" id=\"mwFPY\">write-in</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt3483\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-NM2026_132-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"NM2026\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-NM2026-132\" id=\"mwFPc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFPg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFPk\">[</span>109<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFPo\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt3484\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFPs\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"44\" id=\"mwFPw\" aria-labelledby=\"North_Carolina\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"North_Carolina\">North Carolina</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_Senate_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=44\" title=\"Edit section: North Carolina\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3485\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFP0\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"North Carolina election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"North Carolina\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2020 United States Senate election in North Carolina\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2020\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2032 United States Senate election in North Carolina\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"&apos;&apos;2032&apos;&apos;\"},\"election_date\":{\"wt\":\"&lt;!--Don&apos;t need election date in section infoboxes when the date is the same as in the article&apos;s main infobox.-->\"},\"image_size\":{\"wt\":\"125x136px\"},\"turnout\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"Michael Whatley (55505282618) (cropped).jpg\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Michael Whatley]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"Roy Cooper at Roy Cooper Rally April 2026-2 (cropped).jpg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"[[Roy Cooper]]\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_image\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_size\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_caption\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"U.S. Senator\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Thom Tillis]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt3486\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt3487\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt3488\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt3485\" id=\"mwFP4\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">North Carolina election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_North_Carolina.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Flag_of_North_Carolina.svg/60px-Flag_of_North_Carolina.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Flag_of_North_Carolina.svg/120px-Flag_of_North_Carolina.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"750\" data-file-height=\"500\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"33\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_United_States_Senate_election_in_North_Carolina\" title=\"2020 United States Senate election in North Carolina\">2020</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><i>2032</i><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Michael_Whatley_(55505282618)_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Michael_Whatley_(55505282618)_(cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Michael_Whatley_%2855505282618%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Michael_Whatley_%2855505282618%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Michael_Whatley_%2855505282618%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Michael_Whatley_%2855505282618%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1972\" data-file-height=\"2627\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"102\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Roy_Cooper_at_Roy_Cooper_Rally_April_2026-2_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Roy_Cooper_at_Roy_Cooper_Rally_April_2026-2_(cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Roy_Cooper_at_Roy_Cooper_Rally_April_2026-2_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Roy_Cooper_at_Roy_Cooper_Rally_April_2026-2_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Roy_Cooper_at_Roy_Cooper_Rally_April_2026-2_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Roy_Cooper_at_Roy_Cooper_Rally_April_2026-2_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"2177\" data-file-height=\"2899\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"102\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Whatley\" title=\"Michael Whatley\">Michael Whatley</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roy_Cooper\" title=\"Roy Cooper\">Roy Cooper</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_North_Carolina\" title=\"List of United States senators from North Carolina\">U.S. senator</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thom_Tillis\" title=\"Thom Tillis\">Thom Tillis</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3489\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFP8\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 United States Senate election in North Carolina\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt3490\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt3489\" id=\"mwFQA\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_Senate_election_in_North_Carolina\" title=\"2026 United States Senate election in North Carolina\">2026 United States Senate election in North Carolina</a></div>\n\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3491\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFQE\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"See also\",\"href\":\"./Template:See_also\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"List of United States senators from North Carolina\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt3492\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt3491\" id=\"mwFQI\">See also: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_North_Carolina\" title=\"List of United States senators from North Carolina\">List of United States senators from North Carolina</a></div>\n<p id=\"mwFQM\">Two-term Republican <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thom_Tillis\" title=\"Thom Tillis\" id=\"mwFQQ\">Thom Tillis</a>, who was <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_United_States_Senate_election_in_North_Carolina\" title=\"2020 United States Senate election in North Carolina\" id=\"mwFQU\">narrowly reelected in 2020</a> with 48.7% of the vote, announced on June 29, 2025, that he would not seek a third term after facing backlash for voting against <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One_Big_Beautiful_Bill_Act\" title=\"One Big Beautiful Bill Act\" id=\"mwFQY\">One Big Beautiful Bill Act</a>, prompting <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump\" title=\"Donald Trump\" id=\"mwFQc\">Donald Trump</a> to call for a primary challenger.<sup about=\"#mwt3493\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Tillis_69-2\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Tillis\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Tillis-69\" id=\"mwFQg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFQk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFQo\">[</span>46<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFQs\">]</span></span></a></sup> After Tillis withdrew, Trump endorsed former <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_National_Committee\" title=\"Republican National Committee\" id=\"mwFQw\">Republican National Committee</a> chair <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Whatley\" title=\"Michael Whatley\" id=\"mwFQ0\">Michael Whatley</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt3496\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-268\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-268\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-268\" id=\"mwFQ4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFQ8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFRA\">[</span>244<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFRE\">]</span></span></a></sup> who won the Republican nomination, defeating <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Don_Brown_(author,_born_1960)\" title=\"Don Brown (author, born 1960)\" id=\"mwFRI\">Don Brown</a> in the March 3 primary.<sup about=\"#mwt3499\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-269\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-269\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-269\" id=\"mwFRM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFRQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFRU\">[</span>245<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFRY\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwFRc\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lara_Trump\" title=\"Lara Trump\" id=\"mwFRg\">Lara Trump</a>, former co-chair of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_National_Committee\" title=\"Republican National Committee\" id=\"mwFRk\">Republican National Committee</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wilmington,_North_Carolina\" title=\"Wilmington, North Carolina\" id=\"mwFRo\">Wilmington</a> native, was considered a potential candidate to challenge Tillis, but announced she would not run.<sup about=\"#mwt3502\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-270\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-270\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-270\" id=\"mwFRs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFRw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFR0\">[</span>246<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFR4\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwFR8\">On the Democratic side, former <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Representative\" title=\"U.S. Representative\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwFSA\">U.S. Representative</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wiley_Nickel\" title=\"Wiley Nickel\" id=\"mwFSE\">Wiley Nickel</a> declared his candidacy in April 2025.<sup about=\"#mwt3505\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-271\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-271\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-271\" id=\"mwFSI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFSM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFSQ\">[</span>247<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFSU\">]</span></span></a></sup> Former <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Carolina_Governor\" title=\"North Carolina Governor\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwFSY\">Governor</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roy_Cooper\" title=\"Roy Cooper\" id=\"mwFSc\">Roy Cooper</a> entered the race on July 28, 2025.<sup about=\"#mwt3506\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-nc_68-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"nc\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-nc-68\" id=\"mwFSg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFSk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFSo\">[</span>45<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFSs\">]</span></span></a></sup> Nickel withdrew the following day and endorsed Cooper,<sup about=\"#mwt3509\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-272\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-272\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-272\" id=\"mwFSw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFS0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFS4\">[</span>248<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFS8\">]</span></span></a></sup> who later won the Democratic nomination.<sup about=\"#mwt3512\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-:0_67-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\":0\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:0-67\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-:0-67\" id=\"mwFTA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFTE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFTI\">[</span>44<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFTM\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt3513\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFTQ\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"45\" id=\"mwFTU\" aria-labelledby=\"Ohio_(special)\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Ohio_(special)\"><span id=\"Ohio_.28special.29\" typeof=\"mw:FallbackId\"></span>Ohio (special)</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_Senate_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=45\" title=\"Edit section: Ohio (special)\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3514\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFTY\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"Ohio special election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"Ohio\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2022 United States Senate election in Ohio\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2028 United States Senate election in Ohio\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"&apos;&apos;2028&apos;&apos;\"},\"election_date\":{\"wt\":\"&lt;!--Don&apos;t need election date in section infoboxes when the date is the same as in the article&apos;s main infobox.-->\"},\"image_size\":{\"wt\":\"125x136px\"},\"turnout\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"Sen. Jon Husted official portrait, 119th Congress (cropped 2).jpg\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Jon Husted]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"Sherrod Brown 117th Congress (2) (3x4 crop).jpg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"[[Sherrod Brown]]\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_image\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_size\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_caption\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"U.S. Senator\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Jon Husted]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt3515\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt3516\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt3517\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt3514\" id=\"mwFTc\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">Ohio special election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Ohio.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Flag_of_Ohio.svg/60px-Flag_of_Ohio.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Flag_of_Ohio.svg/120px-Flag_of_Ohio.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"520\" data-file-height=\"320\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"31\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_United_States_Senate_election_in_Ohio\" title=\"2022 United States Senate election in Ohio\">2022</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2028_United_States_Senate_election_in_Ohio\" title=\"2028 United States Senate election in Ohio\" class=\"mw-redirect\"><i>2028</i></a><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Sen._Jon_Husted_official_portrait,_119th_Congress_(cropped_2).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Sen._Jon_Husted_official_portrait,_119th_Congress_(cropped_2).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Sen._Jon_Husted_official_portrait%2C_119th_Congress_%28cropped_2%29.jpg/120px-Sen._Jon_Husted_official_portrait%2C_119th_Congress_%28cropped_2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Sen._Jon_Husted_official_portrait%2C_119th_Congress_%28cropped_2%29.jpg/250px-Sen._Jon_Husted_official_portrait%2C_119th_Congress_%28cropped_2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"2633\" data-file-height=\"3511\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"102\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Sherrod_Brown_117th_Congress_(2)_(3x4_crop).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Sherrod_Brown_117th_Congress_(2)_(3x4_crop).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Sherrod_Brown_117th_Congress_%282%29_%283x4_crop%29.jpg/120px-Sherrod_Brown_117th_Congress_%282%29_%283x4_crop%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Sherrod_Brown_117th_Congress_%282%29_%283x4_crop%29.jpg/250px-Sherrod_Brown_117th_Congress_%282%29_%283x4_crop%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1630\" data-file-height=\"2173\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"102\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jon_Husted\" title=\"Jon Husted\">Jon Husted</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sherrod_Brown\" title=\"Sherrod Brown\">Sherrod Brown</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Ohio\" title=\"List of United States senators from Ohio\">U.S. senator</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jon_Husted\" title=\"Jon Husted\">Jon Husted</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3518\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFTg\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 United States Senate special election in Ohio\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt3519\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt3518\" id=\"mwFTk\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_Senate_special_election_in_Ohio\" title=\"2026 United States Senate special election in Ohio\">2026 United States Senate special election in Ohio</a></div>\n\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3520\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFTo\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"See also\",\"href\":\"./Template:See_also\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"List of United States senators from Ohio\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt3521\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt3520\" id=\"mwFTs\">See also: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Ohio\" title=\"List of United States senators from Ohio\">List of United States senators from Ohio</a></div>\n<p id=\"mwFTw\">One-term Republican <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JD_Vance\" title=\"JD Vance\" id=\"mwFT0\">JD Vance</a> was <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_United_States_Senate_election_in_Ohio\" title=\"2022 United States Senate election in Ohio\" id=\"mwFT4\">elected in 2022</a> with 53% of the vote.<sup about=\"#mwt3524\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-273\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-273\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-273\" id=\"mwFT8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFUA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFUE\">[</span>249<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFUI\">]</span></span></a></sup> On January 10, 2025, he resigned from the Senate after being elected <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vice_President_of_the_United_States\" title=\"Vice President of the United States\" id=\"mwFUM\">Vice President of the United States</a> in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_United_States_presidential_election\" title=\"2024 United States presidential election\" id=\"mwFUQ\">2024</a>. On January 17, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ohio_Governor\" title=\"Ohio Governor\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwFUU\">Governor</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_DeWine\" title=\"Mike DeWine\" id=\"mwFUY\">Mike DeWine</a> announced that then-<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ohio_Lieutenant_Governor\" title=\"Ohio Lieutenant Governor\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwFUc\">Lieutenant Governor</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jon_Husted\" title=\"Jon Husted\" id=\"mwFUg\">Jon Husted</a> would replace Vance in the Senate.<sup about=\"#mwt3527\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-274\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-274\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-274\" id=\"mwFUk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFUo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFUs\">[</span>250<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFUw\">]</span></span></a></sup> Husted is running to serve the remainder of Vance's term.<sup about=\"#mwt3530\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Husted_275-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Husted\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Husted-275\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Husted-275\" id=\"mwFU0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFU4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFU8\">[</span>251<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFVA\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwFVE\">Former U.S. Senator <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sherrod_Brown\" title=\"Sherrod Brown\" id=\"mwFVI\">Sherrod Brown</a>, who was unseated <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Ohio\" title=\"2024 United States Senate election in Ohio\" id=\"mwFVM\">in 2024</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt3533\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-BrownAP_276-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"BrownAP\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BrownAP-276\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-BrownAP-276\" id=\"mwFVQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFVU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFVY\">[</span>252<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFVc\">]</span></span></a></sup> defeated IT professional Ron Kincaid in the Democratic primary on May 5, 2026.<sup about=\"#mwt3536\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-277\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-277\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-277\" id=\"mwFVg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFVk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFVo\">[</span>253<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFVs\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwFVw\">Former <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Libertarian_National_Committee\" title=\"Libertarian National Committee\" id=\"mwFV0\">Libertarian National Committee</a> chair William Redpath is running as a Libertarian.<sup about=\"#mwt3539\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-278\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-278\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-278\" id=\"mwFV4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFV8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFWA\">[</span>254<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFWE\">]</span></span></a></sup> Ohio Libertarians disqualified healthcare consultant Jeffrey Kanter from the Libertarian primary after he submitted hundreds of invalid signatures with his candidate petition.<sup about=\"#mwt3542\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-279\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-279\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-279\" id=\"mwFWI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFWM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFWQ\">[</span>255<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFWU\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt3543\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFWY\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"46\" id=\"mwFWc\" aria-labelledby=\"Oklahoma\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Oklahoma\">Oklahoma</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_Senate_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=46\" title=\"Edit section: Oklahoma\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3544\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFWg\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"Oklahoma election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"Oklahoma\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2022 United States Senate special election in Oklahoma\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2032 United States Senate election in Oklahoma\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"&apos;&apos;2032&apos;&apos;\"},\"election_date\":{\"wt\":\"&lt;!--Don&apos;t need election date in section infoboxes when the date is the same as in the article&apos;s main infobox.-->\"},\"image_size\":{\"wt\":\"125x136px\"},\"turnout\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"Rep. Kevin Hern official photo, 116th congress (cropped).jpg\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Kevin Hern]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"3x4.svg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"N&apos;Kiyla Jasmine Thomas\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_image\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_size\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_caption\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"U.S. Senator\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Alan Armstrong]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt3545\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt3546\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt3547\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt3544\" id=\"mwFWk\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">Oklahoma election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Oklahoma.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Flag_of_Oklahoma.svg/60px-Flag_of_Oklahoma.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Flag_of_Oklahoma.svg/120px-Flag_of_Oklahoma.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"675\" data-file-height=\"450\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"33\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_United_States_Senate_special_election_in_Oklahoma\" title=\"2022 United States Senate special election in Oklahoma\">2022</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><i>2032</i><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Rep._Kevin_Hern_official_photo,_116th_congress_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Rep._Kevin_Hern_official_photo,_116th_congress_(cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Rep._Kevin_Hern_official_photo%2C_116th_congress_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Rep._Kevin_Hern_official_photo%2C_116th_congress_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Rep._Kevin_Hern_official_photo%2C_116th_congress_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Rep._Kevin_Hern_official_photo%2C_116th_congress_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"2159\" data-file-height=\"3028\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"97\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/120px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/250px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"3\" data-file-height=\"4\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"136\" width=\"102\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kevin_Hern\" title=\"Kevin Hern\">Kevin Hern</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">N'Kiyla Jasmine Thomas</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Oklahoma\" title=\"List of United States senators from Oklahoma\">U.S. senator</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alan_Armstrong\" title=\"Alan Armstrong\">Alan Armstrong</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3548\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFWo\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 United States Senate election in Oklahoma\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt3549\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt3548\" id=\"mwFWs\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_Senate_election_in_Oklahoma\" title=\"2026 United States Senate election in Oklahoma\">2026 United States Senate election in Oklahoma</a></div>\n\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3550\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFWw\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"See also\",\"href\":\"./Template:See_also\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"List of United States senators from Oklahoma\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt3551\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt3550\" id=\"mwFW0\">See also: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Oklahoma\" title=\"List of United States senators from Oklahoma\">List of United States senators from Oklahoma</a></div>\n<p id=\"mwFW4\">Incumbent Republican <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Markwayne_Mullin\" title=\"Markwayne Mullin\" id=\"mwFW8\">Markwayne Mullin</a> won <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_United_States_Senate_special_election_in_Oklahoma\" title=\"2022 United States Senate special election in Oklahoma\" id=\"mwFXA\">a special election in 2022</a> with 61.8% of the vote to complete the remainder of the term vacated by <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jim_Inhofe\" title=\"Jim Inhofe\" id=\"mwFXE\">Jim Inhofe</a>, who resigned on January 3, 2023, due to declining health and died in 2024.<sup about=\"#mwt3554\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-280\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-280\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-280\" id=\"mwFXI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFXM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFXQ\">[</span>256<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFXU\">]</span></span></a></sup></p> \n\n<p id=\"mwFXY\">Mullin initially announced plans to seek his first full term in office, but on March 5, 2026, President Trump announced his nomination of Mullin for <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Secretary_of_Homeland_Security\" title=\"United States Secretary of Homeland Security\" id=\"mwFXc\">Secretary of Homeland Security</a>; the Senate confirmed Mullin on March 23.<sup about=\"#mwt3557\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Mullin_281-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Mullin\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Mullin-281\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Mullin-281\" id=\"mwFXg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFXk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFXo\">[</span>257<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFXs\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_Oklahoma\" title=\"Governor of Oklahoma\" id=\"mwFXw\">Governor</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kevin_Stitt\" title=\"Kevin Stitt\" id=\"mwFX0\">Kevin Stitt</a> appointed board member and former CEO of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Williams_Companies\" title=\"Williams Companies\" id=\"mwFX4\">Williams Companies</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alan_Armstrong\" title=\"Alan Armstrong\" id=\"mwFX8\">Alan Armstrong</a> to replace Mullin in the Senate.<sup about=\"#mwt3560\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-282\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-282\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-282\" id=\"mwFYA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFYE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFYI\">[</span>258<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFYM\">]</span></span></a></sup> Armstrong was sworn in on March 24<sup about=\"#mwt3563\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-283\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-283\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-283\" id=\"mwFYQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFYU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFYY\">[</span>259<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFYc\">]</span></span></a></sup> and was required to sign an oath stating that he would not run in the 2026 election.<sup about=\"#mwt3566\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-284\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-284\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-284\" id=\"mwFYg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFYk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFYo\">[</span>260<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFYs\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt3567\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-OK_Statutes_25-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"OK Statutes\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-OK_Statutes-25\" id=\"mwFYw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFY0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFY4\">[</span>14<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFY8\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwFZA\">U.S. Representative for <span data-sort-value=\"Oklahoma01 !\" about=\"#mwt3568\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFZE\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ushr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ushr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"OK\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"1\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oklahoma's_1st_congressional_district\" title=\"Oklahoma's 1st congressional district\">Oklahoma's 1st congressional district</a></span> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kevin_Hern\" title=\"Kevin Hern\" id=\"mwFZI\">Kevin Hern</a><sup about=\"#mwt3571\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Hern11_285-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Hern11\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Hern11-285\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Hern11-285\" id=\"mwFZM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFZQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFZU\">[</span>261<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFZY\">]</span></span></a></sup> won the June 16 Republican primary with 70% of the vote in a crowded field.<sup about=\"#mwt3574\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-:2_286-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\":2\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:2-286\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-:2-286\" id=\"mwFZc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFZg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFZk\">[</span>262<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFZo\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwFZs\">In the June 16 Democratic primary, mediator Jim Priest<sup about=\"#mwt3577\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-287\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-287\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-287\" id=\"mwFZw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFZ0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFZ4\">[</span>263<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFZ8\">]</span></span></a></sup> and nurse N'Kiyla \"Jasmine\" Thomas<sup about=\"#mwt3580\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-ThomasOK_288-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"ThomasOK\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ThomasOK-288\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-ThomasOK-288\" id=\"mwFaA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFaE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFaI\">[</span>264<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFaM\">]</span></span></a></sup> received the most votes and advanced to an August 25 runoff.<sup about=\"#mwt3583\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-289\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-289\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-289\" id=\"mwFaQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFaU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFaY\">[</span>265<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFac\">]</span></span></a></sup> Thomas, a member of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Socialists_of_America\" title=\"Democratic Socialists of America\" id=\"mwFag\">Democratic Socialists of America</a>, won the runoff with 61% of the vote.</p><p id=\"mwFak\">\n\nEntering Wedge Media executive director Ron Meinhardt and pharmacist Curtis Stinnett are running as independents.<sup about=\"#mwt3585\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-:2_286-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\":2\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-:2-286\" id=\"mwFao\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFas\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFaw\">[</span>262<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFa0\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt3588\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-290\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-290\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-290\" id=\"mwFa4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFa8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFbA\">[</span>266<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFbE\">]</span></span></a></sup> Sevier White, candidate for <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oklahoma's_4th_congressional_district\" title=\"Oklahoma's 4th congressional district\" id=\"mwFbI\">Oklahoma's 4th congressional district</a> in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2016_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Oklahoma#District_4\" title=\"2016 United States House of Representatives elections in Oklahoma\" id=\"mwFbM\">2016</a>, is running as a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Libertarian_Party_of_Oklahoma\" title=\"Libertarian Party of Oklahoma\" id=\"mwFbQ\">Libertarian</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt3589\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-:2_286-2\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\":2\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-:2-286\" id=\"mwFbU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFbY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFbc\">[</span>262<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFbg\">]</span></span></a></sup></p><div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt3584\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFbk\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"47\" id=\"mwFbo\" aria-labelledby=\"Oregon\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Oregon\">Oregon</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_Senate_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=47\" title=\"Edit section: Oregon\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3590\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFbs\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"Oregon election\"},\