 title=\"Jack Reed (Rhode Island politician)\">Jack Reed</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Raymond McKay</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Rhode_Island\" title=\"List of United States senators from Rhode Island\">U.S. senator</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jack_Reed_(Rhode_Island_politician)\" title=\"Jack Reed (Rhode Island politician)\">Jack Reed</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3619\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFeU\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 United States Senate election in Rhode Island\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt3620\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt3619\" id=\"mwFeY\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_Senate_election_in_Rhode_Island\" title=\"2026 United States Senate election in Rhode Island\">2026 United States Senate election in Rhode Island</a></div>\n\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3621\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFec\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"See also\",\"href\":\"./Template:See_also\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"List of United States senators from Rhode Island\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt3622\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt3621\" id=\"mwFeg\">See also: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Rhode_Island\" title=\"List of United States senators from Rhode Island\">List of United States senators from Rhode Island</a></div>\n<p id=\"mwFek\">Five-term Democrat <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jack_Reed_(Rhode_Island_politician)\" title=\"Jack Reed (Rhode Island politician)\" id=\"mwFeo\">Jack Reed</a> was <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_United_States_Senate_election_in_Rhode_Island\" title=\"2020 United States Senate election in Rhode Island\" id=\"mwFes\">reelected in 2020</a> with 66.5% of the vote and is running for a sixth term.<sup about=\"#mwt3625\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-JackReed_296-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"JackReed\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-JackReed-296\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-JackReed-296\" id=\"mwFew\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFe0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFe4\">[</span>272<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFe8\">]</span></span></a></sup> He won the Democratic primary on September 9,<sup about=\"#mwt3628\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-:10_297-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\":10\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:10-297\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-:10-297\" id=\"mwFfA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFfE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFfI\">[</span>273<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFfM\">]</span></span></a></sup> defeating elder care worker Connor Burbridge<sup about=\"#mwt3631\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-BurbridgeRI_298-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"BurbridgeRI\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BurbridgeRI-298\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-BurbridgeRI-298\" id=\"mwFfQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFfU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFfY\">[</span>274<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFfc\">]</span></span></a></sup> and physician Luis Daniel Muñoz.<sup about=\"#mwt3634\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-299\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-299\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-299\" id=\"mwFfg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFfk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFfo\">[</span>275<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFfs\">]</span></span></a></sup></p> \n\n<p id=\"mwFfw\">Former <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhode_Island_Republican_Party\" title=\"Rhode Island Republican Party\" id=\"mwFf0\">Rhode Island Republican Party</a> official Raymond McKay is the Republican nominee.<sup about=\"#mwt3635\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-:10_297-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\":10\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-:10-297\" id=\"mwFf4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFf8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFgA\">[</span>273<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFgE\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt3636\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFgI\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"49\" id=\"mwFgM\" aria-labelledby=\"South_Carolina\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"South_Carolina\">South Carolina</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_Senate_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=49\" title=\"Edit section: South Carolina\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt3637\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwFgQ\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"South Carolina election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"South Carolina\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2020 United States Senate election in South Carolina\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2020\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2032 United States Senate election in South Carolina\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"2032\"},\"image_size\":{\"wt\":\"125x136px\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"Official portrait of Darline Graham, member of the United States Senate from South Carolina (2026) (cropped) 2.jpg\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Darline Graham]]\"}